note exit trap6fw: a firmware call needs 64 KiB of the program's stack. Seven 1 MiB frames leave
note about 1 MiB. quiet takes 1000000 more bytes and returns (the frame fits; 8 is printed after it
note returned). loud takes the same frame and then prints: about 48 KiB are left, so efi 13 is
note trap 6 (0000006A) before any firmware call and 9 is never printed.
fn quiet to ulong
a = new uchar 1000000 0
ret add 8 ulong get a 999999
end

fn loud to ulong
a = new uchar 1000000 0
hx add 9 ulong get a 999999
ret 9
end

fn down d ulong to ulong
a = new uchar 1048576 0
put a 0 uchar d
hx add d ulong get a 1048575
if eq d 7
hx quiet
hx loud
end
ret add 1 down add d 1
end

fn main to ulong
mark 66
hx down 1
mark 69
ret 0
end
